## <div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Robots – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 0;"><i>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</i></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Robots on Earth and in Space</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How Robots Are Used in Panama</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Summarize discussions from academic texts. Reading: Extract information from reports on researched topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can summarize academic texts on robotics, identifying key concepts (e.g., "The text explains that robots are used to automate repetitive tasks, improving efficiency in industries like manufacturing and healthcare.")<br>Can extract information from reports on technology in Panama (e.g., "The report shows that robots are increasingly being used in Panama's healthcare sector to assist with surgery and patient care.")<br>Can discuss findings from reports on technology and space (e.g., "The report explains how NASA's Mars rover collects samples autonomously and compares it to local Panamanian projects using drones to monitor biodiversity.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a world map and a few images of robots (e.g., a surgical robot, a drone for agriculture, a Mars rover). Students volunteer to point to Panama on the map and guess how robots might be used in these local contexts based on the images. The teacher asks, "What kinds of robots have you heard about being used here in Panama?" This activates prior knowledge and connects to the theme "How Robots Are Used in Panama."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models effective reading strategies such as skimming for main ideas and scanning for specific information. The teacher also models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words from Lesson 1 (e.g., /r/ in "robot," "research"; /s/ in "space," "sensors") and past participle endings that will appear in the text (e.g., "controlled" /d/, "launched" /t/, "operated" /ɪd/). The teacher explains that today's lesson will involve reading academic texts and reports on robotics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a text is about 'automation,' what does it usually describe?" (Expected: Machines doing tasks without human control.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When we 'extract information' from a report, are we writing a new story or finding specific facts?" (Expected: Finding specific facts.)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Robots on Earth and in Space."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An excerpt from an academic report titled "Robotics in Panama: Advancements in Industry and Agriculture" and a short news article on "Space Exploration: NASA's Martian Mission." The texts will be approximately 250-300 words each, targeting a B1.3 reading level. The texts will include vocabulary such as <i>robot, technology, automation, industry, agriculture, medicine, factory, machine, program, control, sensor, space, astronaut, satellite, planet, mission, orbit, research, exploration</i>. Grammar structures like future perfect ("By 2030, AI will have transformed industries."), passive voice ("Data is collected by robots for analysis."), and zero conditional ("If robots are programmed, they perform with precision.") will be present.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading: Summarize discussions from academic texts. Reading: Extract information from reports on researched topics.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Reading:</b> Students read both texts quickly to identify the main topic of each.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the general focus of the first text?" (A. Robotics in Panamanian sectors / B. The history of robots in space)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which text discusses distant planets?" (A. Text 1 / B. Text 2)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Statements:</b> Students read the texts more carefully and decide if statements are true or false, correcting the false ones.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Robots are currently being used in Panama's agriculture for pest control." (True/False)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"NASA's mission to Mars involves human astronauts collecting samples." (True/False)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension, identifying key concepts, extracting specific information, understanding future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional structures in academic texts. Focus on vocabulary: <i>robot, technology, automation, industry, agriculture, medicine, factory, machine, program, control, sensor, repair, safety, space, astronaut, satellite, rocket, planet, mission, orbit, telescope, research, gravity, universe, galaxy, exploration, station, equipment; launch, program, operate, explore, discover, orbit, repair, control, collect; automated, efficient, mechanical, useful, distant, unexplored, mysterious, space-related.</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> Students receive sentences with blanks that need to be filled with words directly from the texts or target vocabulary (e.g., "In Panama, robots are increasingly used in ______ and ______ to improve efficiency." or "If a robot's ______ detects an obstacle, it will stop automatically."). Other exercises include identifying sentences using the passive voice ("Data is collected by robots for analysis.") or future perfect ("By 2040, robots will have performed most complex surgeries.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled - Information Extraction Grid:</b> Students work individually to complete a grid based on the texts. The grid columns include: "Robot Type/Application," "Location (Panama/Space)," "Purpose/Function," "Key Technology Used," "Potential Future Impact (using Future Perfect)," and "Process (using Passive Voice/Zero Conditional)." E.g., for "Agriculture in Panama," they might list "Drones," "Panama," "Pest control, crop monitoring," "Sensors," "By 2030, drones will have optimized crop yields," "If conditions are adverse, drones collect data."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Discussion & Peer Check:</b> Students form pairs and compare their completed grids. They discuss any discrepancies in their extracted information, clarifying points by re-reading specific sections of the texts. They practice using the target vocabulary and grammatical structures as they discuss, e.g., one student might ask, "According to the report, why might some people worry about the rise of robotics in certain industries in Panama?" and the other responds, referring to the text. They also practice pronunciation of words like "controlled" /d/ and "launched" /t/ when discussing actions mentioned in the text.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Robots on Earth and in Space."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Group Summary & Discussion.</b> Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group is tasked with creating a concise summary (5-7 sentences) of the main findings from both texts, highlighting how robots are used in Panama and comparing it to space exploration. They must explicitly include examples of future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional from the texts or construct new sentences using these structures based on the information. They also need to address the question: "How can robots help in daily life and industries, based on what we've read?" and acknowledge potential concerns ("Why might some people worry about the rise of robotics?").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups collectively decide on the key concepts and most relevant information to summarize from both texts.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They draft their summary, ensuring it incorporates the required grammatical structures and target vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">During the drafting, they discuss their findings, ensuring all viewpoints (e.g., benefits vs. concerns about automation) are considered, as prompted by the questions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group prepares to orally present their summary to the class, making sure to articulate clearly and practice pronunciation, especially the /r/ and /s/ sounds and -ed endings of verbs like "operated" /ɪd/ in their summaries.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy: Observation Checklist & Peer Assessment.</b> The teacher uses an observation checklist to note group collaboration, reading comprehension, and the inclusion of target language. Each group also conducts a brief peer assessment of another group's summary, focusing on clarity and accuracy.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their summary to the class. The teacher assesses their ability to:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Summarize key concepts from academic texts.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Extract relevant information from reports on technology in Panama and space.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporate future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional structures.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use target vocabulary accurately.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Reading Comprehension & Content:</b> Clear identification of main ideas and specific details from both texts (40%)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Language Use:</b> Accurate use of target vocabulary, future perfect, passive voice, and zero conditional (30%)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity & Organization:</b> Summary is coherent, logical, and easy to understand (20%)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration & Participation:</b> Group members actively contributed to the summary and discussion (10%)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I improved my ability to read by..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I found challenging when summarizing the texts was..."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new insights did you gain about the use of robots in Panama or space after reading today's texts?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident are you now in summarizing academic texts and extracting information? What could make you more confident?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The reading tasks provided ample opportunity for students to interact with academic language and report formats. The information extraction grid was particularly effective in ensuring specific details were noted. Some students struggled with differentiating between the passive voice and simple past tense, which will require further reinforcement. For the next lesson (Speaking & Interaction), I will plan activities that encourage more spontaneous use of the extracted information and target grammar, perhaps through a mini-debate or role-play simulating a panel discussion on robotics, integrating the pragmatic and sociolinguistic functions more explicitly.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction), students will use the information extracted and summarized today to engage in active discussions and debates about the impacts of robotics in Panama and space, practicing their fluency and interaction skills.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">2-3 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>